/code-review high 2026-10-08-release-tasks-bump (round 2)

1. .config/mise/tasks/p/i/release:207 — Full mode runs mise x -- git commit unconditionally, so a release with nothing to stage dies under set -e. p:plugins:release and p:site:release both guard this with git diff --cached --quiet. Scenario: package.json was hand-bumped to 1.1.2 and merged, the last tag is installer-v1.1.1, and no installer key is recorded. The task computes target 1.1.2, which equals the manifest, so it writes nothing, and releases_clear finds no key and changes nothing. The index is empty, git commit exits 1 with 'nothing to commit', and the release never reaches the merge or the tag. The same happens when an interrupted run is resumed on develop after the bump commit already landed.
2. .config/mise/tasks/p/plugins/release:189 — The release target is computed from the last tag, not from the manifest, so it can land below the manifest (open gap G1); p:i:release and p:site:release share it. Scenario: last tag vwf-v21.0.0, manifest hand-bumped to 21.2.5, nothing recorded; level_implied MINOR; release_target 21.1.0; plugin.json overwritten downward and published. The table test never covers a manifest more than one step ahead.
3. .config/mise/tasks/p/plugins/release:144 — recorded="$(releases_level ...)" sits outside the refusal guard. A malformed value in releases.yaml kills the task under set -e, even --dry-run, instead of printing '-> refused' and exiting 0. Same in p:i:release and p:site:release. Scenario: a hand edit leaves vwf: major (lowercase) or vwf: "MAJOR"; releases_level returns 1; p:release's planning pass fails with no plan printed.
4. .config/mise/tasks/p/plugins/release:18 — KEYS=(vwf stackgen) hard-codes the plugin list, and the loop skips every other plugin. A third plugin added per 'Adding a Plugin' would never be bumped or tagged; plugins.yml then fails on main with 'marketplace.json pins ... not a tag'. Derive the names from the glob or the marketplace.
5. .config/mise/tasks/p/plugins/release:189 — The bump loop mutates files as it goes (rewrites plugin.json and runs releases_clear per plugin) before all plugins are validated. A later plugin's refusal exits 1 and leaves a half-bumped tree; the next run refuses on 'Working tree is not clean', and the recorded level is lost unless restored by hand. Compute and validate every target first, then write.
6. .github/workflows/deps-update.yml:75 — The monthly job depends on code:merge:main's preconditions and pushes develop before running the release. Any refusal from the merge leaves a pushed, unreleased refresh on develop. The following if ... origin/develop..develop check can never fire after a successful push, so it is dead code.
7. .config/mise/tasks/p/plugins/release:150 — The last-tag lookup, level, target, refuse-or-skip, merge-model check, clean-tree check, fetch and EXIT-trap logic is copy-pasted across the three release tasks, with small drifts between the copies. The common step could be one function in _scripts/local.
8. .config/mise/tasks/p/release:95 — p:release runs the heavy gates (p:i:test, p:site:check) before the bump, and the --tag-only steps on main run the same gates again. Every release pays for each gate twice.
9. .config/vwf.yaml:1 — The new .config/vwf.yaml holds only after_landing. Creating it flips the repo from 'not onboarded' to onboarded for vwf's config-driven commands such as doctor, which will then expect the remaining required keys. The plan's decision E10 chose this deliberately, but nothing shows the consumers tolerate a partial file.
10. CLAUDE.md:1 — The branch changes release behavior with no doc changes in the same commits; the plan defers this to U7 in wave 5.
